  "id": "timelocation-sampling",
  "term": "time–location sampling",
  "definition": "Time–location sampling is a way of recruiting a study sample by selecting particular sites and then sampling people at those places during set time periods. In the example provided, it used a stratified, multistage probability design in which WIC sites were chosen first and newly enrolled participants were then sampled within selected sites during planned recruitment windows.",
